    [38;2;197;201;199mYou're right, per the mod docs. A mod can message a finished subagent by its id, and the engine wakes that same agent from its transcript with the message. A mod also sees each workflow agent[39m
    [38;2;197;201;199mstart and learns its id.[39m

    [38;2;197;201;199mSo the route: the mod records each workflow reviewer's id as it starts. When a review needs another pass, the script calls a small tool the mod provides, which messages that same reviewer and[39m
    [38;2;197;201;199mhands back its answer. The reviewer comes back warm, with everything it already read.[39m

    [38;2;197;201;199mOne fact is open. The docs say workflow agents don't appear in the mod's agent list, so I don't know yet whether the engine accepts a workflow agent's id for that message. A tiny test mod[39m
    [38;2;197;201;199msettles it: a workflow with one agent, then the mod wakes it with a follow-up. Should I build that test?[39m

